## 7. NAVIGATION — REMOVE BOTTOM TABS, USE A MENU
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

**Remove the bottom tab bar completely.** It's crowded. Replace with this:

### 7.1 Home is the hub
The Home screen becomes the central dashboard. From Home, the user reaches
everything either through content cards (primary actions surfaced directly) or
through the menu (everything else).

### 7.2 The menu
A top-right menu button on the Home screen (and a back arrow on all sub-screens).

Menu button: a 48px circular white button, Shadow.soft, with a Feather 'menu'
icon (24px, ink colour), top-right of the Home header.

Tapping it opens a **slide-in drawer from the right** (or a bottom sheet on
smaller devices — your call, drawer preferred). The drawer:
- Covers ~82% of screen width, warm background #FDFAF8
- Soft shadow on its left edge
- At the top: the user's avatar (orange circle, initials), name in serif, email
- Then a generously spaced list of menu items, each a ListRow with:
  - A Feather icon in an orange-tint rounded square (44px) on the left
  - Label in 16px medium
  - Chevron right
  - 20px vertical padding per row (roomy)

Menu items in order:
```
My Journey        (map icon)       → questionnaire hub / progress
My Results        (bar-chart-2)    → results dashboard
My Plan           (list)           → personalised plan
My Orders         (shopping-bag)   → order history & tracking
Appointments      (calendar)       → appointments list
Shop              (grid)           → store
Weekly Goals      (target)         → goals screen
Recipes           (coffee)         → recipes
Profile           (user)           → profile
Settings          (settings)       → settings
Help & Support    (help-circle)    → support
```

- A divider, then "Log out" in red at the bottom.
- Each item has 20px vertical padding — the menu must feel spacious, not listy.

### 7.3 Navigation pattern
- Home → menu → any section (pushes onto the stack)
- Every sub-screen has a back arrow top-left (48px circular white button,
  Shadow.soft, Feather 'arrow-left', ink colour)
- Deep actions from Home cards go straight to the relevant screen
- No bottom bar anywhere. The screen is cleaner and more spacious without it.

### 7.4 Implementation
- Remove the `(tabs)` layout / Tabs navigator from expo-router
- Use a Stack navigator with Home as the root
- Build the drawer as a reusable component `components/navigation/MenuDrawer.tsx`
  using react-native-reanimated for the slide-in, or a modal with a slide animation
- Keep all the existing screen routes — only the navigation chrome changes

